WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.500
A human has 518 protein kinases.

2
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.280
Baker's yeast has roughly 120 to 130.

3
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.640
Animals share a short list of signaling pathways, so where did the extra parts come

4
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.280
from? The record does not show animals inventing one new pathway after another.

5
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:26.020
Kinase totals roughly track genome size, but the receptors multiplied more than the

6
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.020
core.

7
00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:31.183
Mistakes in copying DNA sometimes duplicate a single gene.

8
00:00:31.723 --> 00:00:33.383
Say a receptor gene is copied.

9
00:00:33.943 --> 00:00:37.583
The original keeps doing the job, so the spare copy is free to change.

10
00:00:38.323 --> 00:00:41.923
A fly has one EGF receptor and a human has four.

11
00:00:42.763 --> 00:00:47.283
Jawed vertebrates carry traces of two whole genome doublings, the likely route from

12
00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:48.283
one to four.

13
00:00:48.917 --> 00:00:51.237
A spare copy has three main fates.

14
00:00:51.657 --> 00:00:52.817
The common one is loss.

15
00:00:53.417 --> 00:00:58.157
A mutation disables the copy, nothing selects against that, and it decays into a

16
00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:02.037
pseudogene. In the second fate, the copies divide the old job.

17
00:01:02.717 --> 00:01:05.357
Suppose the old receptor worked in gut and in nerve.

18
00:01:05.937 --> 00:01:11.037
If one copy loses the regulatory DNA for gut and the other loses it for nerve, the

19
00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.037
animal needs both.

20
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.540
In the third fate, one copy takes a new job.

21
00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:20.400
Its tail may change, so a different set of tyrosines recruits different SH2

22
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.940
proteins. A docking site is only a few amino acids.

23
00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:30.780
The SH2 domains of PI 3-kinase read a phosphotyrosine followed three positions later

24
00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.720
by methionine. One or two point mutations in the tail can make such a site, and with

25
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.680
it a line to PI 3-kinase.

26
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:41.163
Now carry the duplication through a whole pathway.

27
00:01:41.843 --> 00:01:46.383
In one outcome, everything downstream is copied too, and the four cascades stay

28
00:01:46.383 --> 00:01:47.563
apart like four wires.

29
00:01:48.323 --> 00:01:51.783
In the other, the receptors go on sharing downstream parts and gain

30
00:01:51.783 --> 00:01:52.783
cross-connections.

31
00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:56.523
Many inputs then funnel into a few hubs, and Ras is one.

32
00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:01.723
The counts fit shared wiring, but they cannot show it, and the core was copied too.

33
00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:05.667
So the extra kinases are not a list of new pathways.

34
00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:11.067
The record shows old pathways copied, mostly at the receptor end, and the copies

35
00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:16.947
changed. New wiring can cost only a few amino acids, because signaling proteins are

36
00:02:16.947 --> 00:02:18.667
built from parts that work on their own.

37
00:02:19.387 --> 00:02:23.607
Keep this rule: old pathways get copied, and the copies get rewired.
